{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-syntomic-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a485103d8e345949583845ab84774932064aba5660e05e1ba58fd4e89373c6c", "source_text": "A syntomic morphism is universally open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1497b83dc1319d91a4b5f12fd32016ab26187e4b18501de3e7ec2e1c06fd5bbe", "unit_id": "tag:056F:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-syntomic-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-syntomic-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e164d2be7144fa37c229ec382f3787f38962798ba5bd9f7b117b1169672e87f4", "source_text": "Combine\nLemmas <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70dd06ef4c7c53c782b6828cef94c9caeb72e012863e931fa73b52e5bd3486df", "unit_id": "tag:056F:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$k$", "MATH_0007": "$A \\cong R/(f_1, \\ldots, f_c)$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "MATH_0009": "$k$", "MATH_0010": "$f_1, \\ldots, f_c$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-lci-local-ring}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:849216119895ccb7058939ba501ccdb41811ca23d25b5fb8d942f2a31ea01d9b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e472e6390786da296f041e0b283391506a075c85a92c1f62a0caab9ebc6702ef", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a field. Let <MATH_0002> be a local <MATH_0003>-algebra essentially\nof finite type over <MATH_0004>. Recall that <MATH_0005> is called a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>complete intersection over <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if we can write\n<MATH_0007> where <MATH_0008> is a regular local ring\nessentially of finite type over <MATH_0009>, and <MATH_0010> is\na regular sequence in <MATH_0011>, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e15e1c8d53f47ab797a80153033563cf06f22d7d1060d614ed9ca210d459ed20", "unit_id": "tag:01UB:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$k$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0007": "$U = \\Spec(R) \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$R \\cong k[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/(f_1, \\ldots, f_c)$", "MATH_0010": "$k$", "MATH_0011": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0013": "$k$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-local-complete-intersection}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:547d7260ed2dfc4928f9cbc778422e3d41026df557fec9217c71ce0e5a914d5d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c911f8bad296f71f9f71883909e0e31cbd96ee7390740464abb741c3569c489", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a field.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme locally of finite type over <MATH_0003>.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is a local complete intersection over <MATH_0005>,\n<STRUCT_0003> for every <MATH_0006> there exists an affine open\n<MATH_0007> neighbourhood of <MATH_0008>\nsuch that <MATH_0009>\nis a global complete intersection over <MATH_0010>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for every <MATH_0011> the local ring <MATH_0012>\nis a complete intersection over <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b1d4db277691b4856044fc4ae859420637dc1ef84904bfa35c380e3729ae3e9", "unit_id": "tag:01UG:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-lci-at-prime}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-lci-global}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c5c955dde2f7d415cc489a3c967ed67f9f539793e0d1a51a17da634e1ed9b1ff", "source_text": "The corresponding algebra results can be found in\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bab6986299266124f053ea27b01fa5c050d12e70a7c7a19460a526aa0b85130e", "unit_id": "tag:01UG:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01UB", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f7a2d4910119b447244cfef2dbd06e9c94c947ea42ee0be63bf7577218f41ed1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma says locally any syntomic morphism is standard syntomic.\nHence we can use standard syntomic morphisms as a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>local model<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nfor a syntomic morphism. Moreover, it says that a flat morphism of finite\npresentation is syntomic if and only if the fibres are local complete\nintersection schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b37d6cd66b19782f01b22e4991e61eae6ad16fe69a9d0d706082f35862b60099", "unit_id": "tag:01UB:prose-0004"}
